    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0341" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4190</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Polish Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sokolowski</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <p>The Chargé d’Affaires ad interim of Poland presents his compliments to the Acting
                    Secretary of State, and referring to his enquiry of June 25, 1931,<anchor n="25"
                        xml:id="d185-f1"/> as to the attitude of the Polish Government towards the
                    proposal of President Hoover published in the general press on June 20th and
                    21st, has the honor to inform him that the Polish Government welcomes with the
                    highest appreciation the noble initiative of President Hoover, in the belief
                    that it will be coincident with a general political relaxation, and regards such
                    initiative as an important step towards the stabilization of Peace.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1931-06-27">June 27,
                            1931</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>No. 168/T/31</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
